properties.statement:
When a claim's support is a hypothesis test (a kept calc record of a named test):
- its reading names α, the p-value, the test and n;
- it is never shown, proven or holds;
- a non-significant result reads "not rejected at α";
- the test's assumptions (normality, independence, expected counts) are premises of the step, so an objection can attack them;
- the read-back keeps "evidence, not proof", as reflow2 already rules (fact:the-methods-of-proof-mostly-fit-an-inference-and-three-need-more-2026-10-14).
Option (b) of flo2-calc's dec:idea-how-a-statistical-hypothesis-test-is-designed-computed-and-read, kept with (a).
